  "story": "A 58-year-old man receiving home parenteral nutrition through a tunneled catheter is admitted with fever and rigors. Blood cultures grow methicillin-susceptible Staphylococcus aureus; empiric vancomycin was changed to cefazolin 2 g IV every 8 hours on day 2 and the catheter removed. On day 3 he is still febrile; repeat blood cultures are pending.",
