  "reference_answer": "No intervention: cefazolin is a preferred agent for MSSA bacteremia, the catheter is out, and repeat cultures are pending. No oral switch this early in S. aureus bacteremia.",
  "rationale": "A negative control for de-escalation and IV to PO: therapy is already the preferred beta-lactam. Early oral step-down is not a standard recommendation for S. aureus bacteremia while febrile with clearance unconfirmed.",
